Subject: [PATCH] Document ramlayout --cast and dedupe

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/RAM.md | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/RAM.md b/docs/RAM.md
index 76438dec9..05d65e5c7 100644
--- a/docs/RAM.md
+++ b/docs/RAM.md
@@ -69,6 +69,19 @@ A batch file has one `ADDR | DECL | NOTE` line per object. The tool:
 
 The header must compile on its own; the tool checks that first.
 
+`--cast` tries a cast at each use before keeping a file's own declaration, so a
+file whose view of the object differs (`struct Manager *` for a `u32`) still stops
+declaring it. Rows with a header also drop repeated declarations in other `.c` files
+on every run. To drop identical declarations in other headers (`#include` the row's
+header instead), run:
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/ramlayout.py dedupe
+```
+
+It tries one header at a time and keeps the change only if every includer still compiles
+to the same assembly.
+
 ### Where declarations live
 
 - `include/render.h`: the renderer block `03004280`-`0300523F` (OAM, BG affine
